      "abstract": "We measure how closely lantern moths beat their wings in phase. Across forty colonies, synchrony rises with colony size, and it peaks at dusk.",
      "headings": [
        {
          "level": 1,
          "text": "Introduction",
          "locator": "p1",
          "first_sentence": "Lantern moths gather in dusk swarms whose wingbeats lock together [@Okafor2017]."
        },
        {
          "level": 1,
          "text": "Results",
          "locator": "p3",
          "first_sentence": "Larger colonies beat more nearly in phase than small ones (Figure 1)."
        },
        {
          "level": 1,
          "text": "Discussion",
          "locator": "p8",
          "first_sentence": "Our central finding is that synchrony rises with colony size."
        },
        {
          "level": 1,
          "text": "Methods",
          "locator": "p10",
          "first_sentence": "Wingbeats were filmed at 2000 frames per second; the phase of each moth was taken from the analytic signal, as described in methods.tex."
        },
        {
          "level": 1,
          "text": "Acknowledgements",
          "locator": "p12",
          "first_sentence": "We thank the moth keepers of the invented Varga lab."
        },
        {
          "level": 1,
          "text": "References",
          "locator": "p14",
          "first_sentence": "Lindqvist, A. and Moreau, P."
        }
